  "problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-5{y}^{\u2032}+6y=2x{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be written as\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{3x}+g(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants. Which of the following could be the function $g(x)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the variation of parameters method. You may also wish to make use of the following result (integration constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int x{e}^{-x}dx=-(x+1){e}^{-x}\n$$",
